      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two groups of ischemic heart disease patients with different responses to antianginal therapy (propranolol, nifedipine) were studied. Mathematical analysis of heart rate variabilities showed that tolerant patients had a low index of centralization, lack of its circadian rhythm and a low correlation between several cardiointervalographic parameters. Bearing in mind these shifts makes it possible to predict the therapeutical efficiency of the antianginal drugs."},
